          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Just as an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            comes with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            formalized by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} elementary (∞,1)-topos
            should come with its
            %em
              internal “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-logic”
            formalized by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %h2#TypeTheoryVersusLogic Type theory versus logic
          %p
            As remarked at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponentials
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifiers"} object classifiers
            belong to the type theory, while
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                dual images
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/dual+image"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifiers"} subobject classifiers
            belong to the logic. Thus, the semantics of (extensional) type theory naturally lies in a category with appropriate structure, while the semantics of logic over that type theory naturally lies in some indexed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            over that category. However, we commonly take this indexed poset to consist of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            in the category in question, in which case additional “logical” structure on the category is required, for instance that it be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
          %p
            In an elementary 1-topos, all of the “logical” structure is not usually included in the definition, because it comes for free once you have
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+objects"} power objects
            = succeed "-topos," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %h2#the_type_theory_of_an_category
            The type theory of an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Amazingly, a variant of type theory that seems appropriate for interpretation in an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %em intensional type theory
            with
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
          %h3#intensional_identity_types_in_categories
            Intensional identity types in
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The usual sort of type theory that one interprets in a 1-category is
            = succeed "." do
              %em extensional type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times B
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizers"} equalizers
            = succeed "," do
              %em identity types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and each pair of terms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_A(x,y)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x=y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_A(x,y)
            be equal, i.e. that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_A(x,y)
            be essentially a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A\vdash f(x):B
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A\vdash g(x):B
            representing morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g\colon A\to B
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_{x:A} Id_B(f(x),g(x))
          %p
            However, for semantics in an
            = succeed "-category," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space"} path space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_A(x,y)
            is a subsingleton, since two points can be connected by more than one path, so we must drop that axiom. This
            %em intensional type theory
            has been widely studied by type-theorists, although from a different point of view: assuming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            approach,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_A(x,y)
            should be the type of
            %em proofs
            or
            %em reasons
            why
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x=y
          %p
            Thus we suspect that intensional type theory may be a natural sort of type theory to have semantics in an
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ol
            %li
              From any intensional type theory, we can construct a syntactic
              = succeed "-category," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %li
              In any
              = succeed "-category," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Some work in both of these directions has been done. On the one hand, it is known that in any intensional type theory with identity types, for any type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globular+set"} globular set
            (or more accurately globular
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇇
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo ⇇
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mi A
                  %mo ⇇
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \leftleftarrows Id_A \leftleftarrows Id_{Id_A} \leftleftarrows \dots
          %p
            has the structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Batanin+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} Batanin ∞-groupoid
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Lumsdaine"}> Peter Lumsdaine
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Weak omega-categories from intensional type theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.0409"} arXiv:0812.0409
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"} Richard Garner
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"} Benno van den Berg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Types are weak omega-groupoids
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.0298"} arXiv:0812.0298
          %p
            Moreover, the syntactic category of such a theory carries a natural
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system"} weak factorization system
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                identity type weak factorization system
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/identity+type+weak+factorization+system"} ?
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            On the other hand, it is known that in any nice enough
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            (and in fact, in any category with a nice enough
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system"} weak factorization system
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Awodey"} Steve Awodey
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Warren"} Michael Warren
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theoretic models of identity types
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.0248"} arXiv:0709.0248
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Warren"}> Michael Warren
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theoretic aspects of constructive type theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://aix1.uottawa.ca/~mwarren/Papers/phd.pdf"} Ph.D. thesis
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Vladimir Voevodsky
            has also studied the particular model of intensional type theory in simplicial sets, which he calls the
            = succeed ";" do
              %em univalent model
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/~vladimir/Site3/home.html"} website
          %h3#additional_axioms Additional axioms
          %p
            Although intensional type theory has semantics in
            = succeed "-categories," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Exponential (and dependent product) types can probably be modeled by (locally) cartesian closed
                = succeed "-categories." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                = succeed "-extensionality" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %li
              %p
                Disjoint sum types may be expected to correspond to coproducts in an
                = succeed "-category." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %li
              %p
                The usual notions of
                %em quotient type
                make little sense without extensional identity types. In the 1-categorical world, quotient types correspond to
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+categories"} exact categories
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+objects+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid objects in an (∞,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier"} object classifier
                in an
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %em universe
                such as the type
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Type
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Type
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %em paths
                between two types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                as elements of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Type
                (that is, the path space
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mi Type
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_{Type}(A,B)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                as types (an appropriate subspace of the exponential
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Voevodsky
                under the name of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em equivalence axiom
          %h2#logic_over_type_theory_in_an_category
            Logic over type theory in an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Now when we go to add
            %em logic
            to the type theory of an
            = succeed "-category," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %em subobjects
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monomorphisms in an (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(x)
            with a variable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            will be interpreted by a monomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\varphi] \rightarrowtail [A]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of a 1-category and of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/2-categorical+logic"} 2-category
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Again, the requisite type theory more or less exists, namely intensional type theory together with a sort of propositions that can depend on types. In fact, this type theory is very closely related to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+constructions"} calculus of constructions
            used in the proof assistant
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://coq.inria.fr/"} Coq
            = succeed "-topos." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/~vladimir/Site3/home.html"} website
          %h2#the_problem_of_finiteness The problem of finiteness
          %p
            In describing the internal type theory and logic of an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
          %p
            There is the one amazing fact that the entire complicated infinitary structure of a Batanin
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
            in the
            = succeed "-case," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            However, such a type theory would obviously no longer have “computational content” and couldn’t be modeled in a proof assistant such as Coq, and also wouldn’t provide a fully “elementary,” i.e. finitary first-order, theory such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            provides in the 1-categorical case. It might be helpful to note that infinitary structures can at least sometimes be finitarily described using
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+type"} inductive type
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinductive+type"} coinductive type
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#OfInfGrpd
            Internal logic in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd
          %p
            The archetypical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} (∞,1)-categorification
            of the archetypical 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p
            At
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/internal+logic#LogicOfSet"} internal logic - in Set
            is a step-by-step discussion of how ordinary logic is recovered from the point of view of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of a topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            when choosing
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T} := Set
          %p
            Here we look at the
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
              %p
                This
                %em generates
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd
                under
                = succeed "s:" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "-groupoid." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %li
              %p
                The
                %em subobject classifier
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd
                is
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
